# .p4ignore — Perforce ignore file.
#
# Translates .gitignore with p4 syntax differences. Authored per Phase 1 Step 3
# of docs/design/git-to-perforce-migration.md. Critically excludes .git/ so the
# git metadata directory never gets reconciled into the p4 depot.
#
# Syntax notes (Perforce 2014.2+):
#   - gitignore-compatible globs (`*`, `?`, `**`)
#   - `!` negation (later rules override earlier)
#   - leading `/` anchors to client root
#   - trailing `/` matches directories only
#   - `#` line-comments
#
# NOT listed here (intentional): .gitignore itself — it is tracked in git and
# baseline-imported to p4 in Phase 1 Step 4. .p4ignore only governs untracked
# candidates for `p4 add` / `p4 reconcile`.

# ----- Git metadata (must never enter the depot) -----
.git/
.gitignore.swp

# ----- Per-clone p4 client config (host-specific; never committed) -----
# .p4config files override P4PORT / P4USER / P4CLIENT / P4IGNORE per folder.
# Used on machines like Brick that run multiple p4d contexts (e.g. an unrelated
# local p4d for Unreal + Mainbot's depot for Smatchet) where global env vars
# would collide. The file's content is per-clone and must NOT enter the depot.
.p4config

# ----- FetchContent clones / Lua tarball -----
.fetchcontent-src/
/.fetchcontent-msvc

# ----- Build output / cache -----
build/
build_*/
**/CMakeFiles/
**/CMakeCache.txt
**/cmake_install.cmake
**/*.cmake.user
CMakeUserPresets.json
compile_commands.json
/smatchet-cppcheck-build-dir
cppcheck_*.txt

